c - A report from Sr. ITAMIR, Commander of the SEAHORSE Team
Sr. Emmanuel Ruchum, of national origin, telephoned at
16:10 on the 11th of August and reported:
                                  - He was on his way for another mission;
                                  - On the 27th of July 1950, at 19:00F, when the CAIOBA sector called and reported the incident, the SEAHORSE was + one thousand nautical miles behind the CAIOBA;

It reads like that of a literal;

                              - His machine chief and a martial dice say he saw an unusual light, not at all abnormal;
                              - He would have his machine chief stop immediately;
S°/* and
                              - Hand acted with the command of the Chief of Staff about this -
                              - He reports that he was affected by a peculiar intoxication.

As per questions formulated, respond as follows:

. At that time, the Teche (a ship) was located about 3 miles behind and to the west of a point some ... 3 miles away;
. The speed of the Caiora (a vessel) was approximately 0.2 knots;
. The speed of the Teche (a ship) in cross-current was 12 knots;
. It is not known why Arthur Levy sent the immediate message to Salvador, Bahia; "it seems (the reason) was the necessity of an immediate message, in Salvador, for a new ship that arrived in America";
. Arthur Levy from Brazil has been working on this for about 20 months;
. On July 27, 19:30 PM, he transmitted the position of the Caioba (a vessel) to Natal Radio;
. They have confirmed the transmitted position, but under conditions that did not allow him to communicate, nor does he know how he reached the command point at that time;
. The height of the top of the Caioba's mast should be approximately 10 meters above the waterline and about 15 meters above the water level.

Ass. (José Silva)

The impression of a distance of 3,000 nautical miles, at an altitude of 60 meters, with the object measuring twice its diameter apparent from the lunar light, leads to the following conclusions:

a - elevation: 0.02° (that is, one-tenth of a degree);

b - the diameter of the "object", of the light or of the "J70": 100 meters.

- Totally valid, sincere and clear, are the statements of Sr./AH;
- Totally valid is the statement of Sr. Pmmanuel, that he did not see any strange light or unusual movement. What he saw was so far away that it could be perfectly a bird, as he described to Sr. Scarpat;
- Valid are the information about position given by Sr. Fangueiro in his report, up to the time (19:00 hours), "they remain valid from that moment forward, chronologically speaking;
- Not valid are the statements of the Commander of the Air Force regarding the "light" and its movements.

